  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The trade calendar with a live date pad",
    "overview": "The site borrows the printed wall calendar that Indian shops give their customers: a bright picture plate inside a printed frame, the name in a band, and a pad of tear-off date sheets. Each departure is a sheet, and the date is the largest thing on any page. Colour is flat print ink at page scale; names are set in sign lettering and everything functional in a sturdy text face.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "The date sheet is the signature object",
      "Flat inks, square corners, ruled lines",
      "Sign lettering for names only",
      "One column grid shared by every page"
